--- task
id: r11
dataset: reading
kind: delete nodes selected by an anti-join
answer: fewest
composition: a write fed by a read: edition 2's `delete … where` cannot see an anti-join, so the client reads the slugs and deletes by key

--- intent
Delete the documents that nobody knows.

--- edition2
query unknown_docs() {
  match { $d: Doc  not { $p knows $d } }
  return { $d.slug }
}

--- edition2 bind ids=1:d.slug
query drop_docs($ids: [String]) {
  delete Doc where slug in $ids
}

--- edition3
query drop_unknown() {
  $d: Doc
  not { $p knows $d }
  delete $d
}

--- check
query check() {
  match { $d: Doc }
  return { $d.slug }
}

--- expect unordered
columns: ["d.slug"]
["d0"]
["d1"]
["d2"]
